// useSavedCredentials is the one origin gate (handfixes.json
// saved-credentials-stay-with-their-vcenter): a credential saved on disk is used
// only when the vCenter it was saved for is the one this run talks to
// (VSPHERE_BASE_URL, else the config's base_url), compared as origins: scheme
// and host case, the default port and a trailing slash do not count. It applies
// a store's credentials, or keeps the config file's own; otherwise it records a
// refusal, so the command fails rather than send one to another host, and drops
// the config file's credential fields and [headers]. A credential from the
// environment never comes here: it goes where the operator pointed it.
